# Custom-prefix bootstrap pin: emacshell-termux flavor (aarch64).
#
# All Termux packages are compiled with the prefix
# /data/data/com.termux/files/usr hardcoded inside them.  The OFFICIAL
# upstream bootstrap therefore cannot work under emacshell's applicationId
# (tech.khalidrafi.emacshell.termux), which lives at a different data
# directory.  A custom bootstrap must be built from termux-packages with
# TERMUX_APP_PACKAGE=tech.khalidrafi.emacshell.termux; see
# scripts/build-bootstrap.sh and BUILD.org ("Bootstrap prefix rebuild",
# termux issue #24396).
#
# Until that CI job has produced and reviewed a build, this file holds a
# PLACEHOLDER instead of a real pin.  scripts/install-bootstrap (Gradle
# task in app/build.gradle) refuses to build the APK in that state, so a
# wrong-prefix bootstrap can never ship silently.
#
# To fill this in after running scripts/build-bootstrap.sh:
#
#   <sha256 of bootstrap-aarch64.zip>
#
# Layout expected by the build:
#   bootstrap/termux/bootstrap-aarch64.zip     (gitignored build output)
#
# For reference, the OFFICIAL upstream v0.118.3 bootstrap hashes (which
# are com.termux-prefixed and NOT usable here) are, from termux-app
# v0.118.3 app/build.gradle, release 2025.03.28-r1+apt-android-7:
#   aarch64 c8d702b6f742935001c37cda81b8ac69504a95d5cf28f2899532dd8cd4b057eb
#   arm     f3bb9d1b32552b34fff41861dbf193ec5ba2848d67d779ac1c7256da6640f85d
#   i686    36db3e1ac3547f9a174fd763bd9a484fa1a3449cdd81e1cf2408ff0454f839c6
#   x86_64  1c124ec2396ee70a51b0b0a574f29aa659526aa2b9f558f993b2fb05d1e51855

PLACEHOLDER
